1
00:00:01,233 --> 00:00:03,267
- [Narrator] Mystery
Science Theater 3000,

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:05,567
show 412, reel one.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,800
♪ In the
not-too-distant future ♪

4
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:12,267
♪ Next Sunday, A.D. ♪

5
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:15,000
♪ There was a guy named Joel ♪

6
00:00:15,033 --> 00:00:18,367
♪ Not too different
from you or me ♪

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,200
♪ He worked at
Gizmonic Institute ♪

8
00:00:21,233 --> 00:00:24,567
♪ Just another face
in a red jumpsuit ♪

9
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:27,367
♪ He did a good job
cleaning up the place ♪

10
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,867
♪ But his bosses
didn't like him ♪

11
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:33,867
♪ So they shot him into space ♪

12
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:37,000
♪ We'll send him cheesy movies ♪

13
00:00:37,033 --> 00:00:40,167
♪ The worst we can
find, la la la ♪

14
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,100
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

15
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:46,400
♪ And we'll monitor
his mind, la la la ♪

16
00:00:46,433 --> 00:00:49,200
♪ Now keep in mind,
Joel can't control ♪

17
00:00:49,233 --> 00:00:52,433
♪ Where the movies
begin or end, la la la ♪

18
00:00:52,467 --> 00:00:55,533
♪ Because he used
those special parts ♪

19
00:00:55,567 --> 00:01:00,567
♪ To make his robot friends ♪

20
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:02,300
♪ Robot roll call ♪

21
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:03,733
♪ Cambot ♪
- Pan Left.

22
00:01:03,767 --> 00:01:04,967
♪ Gypsy ♪
- Hi, girl.

23
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,700
♪ Tom Servo ♪
- What a cool guy.

24
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:08,433
♪ Crow ♪
- He's a wisecracker.

25
00:01:08,467 --> 00:01:11,233
♪ If you're wondering how
he eats and breathes ♪

26
00:01:11,267 --> 00:01:14,267
♪ And other science
facts, la la la ♪

27
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:17,367
♪ Then repeat to yourself,
it's just a show ♪

28
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:20,600
♪ I should really just relax ♪

29
00:01:20,633 --> 00:01:24,900
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000 ♪

30
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:30,167
(doors whooshing)

31
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:37,267
- But you said that someday

32
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:38,933
I could watch the
movie with you guys!

33
00:01:38,967 --> 00:01:40,900
- Gypsy, come on, you
know I need you to run

34
00:01:40,933 --> 00:01:43,400
the higher functions of the
ship, that's why I created you.

35
00:01:43,433 --> 00:01:45,200
- Yeah, you just
had me so I could do

36
00:01:45,233 --> 00:01:46,467
all the work around here.

37
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,367
- Just a second, hi
everybody, welcome to

38
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,633
the Satellite of Love,
I'm Joel Robinson.

39
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:54,100
Gypsy and I were just
discussing the possibility

40
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:58,100
that maybe she might be included
in this week's experiment.

41
00:01:58,133 --> 00:01:59,400
- Oh, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

42
00:01:59,433 --> 00:02:01,133
- Okay, now Gypsy,
you know that Joel

43
00:02:01,167 --> 00:02:03,200
created you and has
a wonderful plan

44
00:02:03,233 --> 00:02:04,667
for your life, right?
- Yeah.

45
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:06,133
- And on the day he created you,

46
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:09,033
he gave you a special gift
that none of the other robots

47
00:02:09,067 --> 00:02:10,733
on this ship share, right?
- You did?

48
00:02:10,767 --> 00:02:13,400
- Right, and Joel wants
you to use that gift.

49
00:02:13,433 --> 00:02:14,800
- He does?

50
00:02:14,833 --> 00:02:17,000
- Richard Basehart.
- Don't patronize me, Joel!

51
00:02:17,833 --> 00:02:19,033
- Okay.

52
00:02:19,067 --> 00:02:21,033
Have you adjusted the
stabilizers on the ship?

53
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:22,267
- Done!

54
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:23,500
- Okay, have you told
the computer to give us

55
00:02:23,533 --> 00:02:24,867
an uninterrupted
supply of oxygen?

56
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:26,033
- Roger dodger!

57
00:02:26,067 --> 00:02:27,300
- Okay, have you
taken the heat shields

58
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:29,367
and pointed 'em up to the sun?
- Yep, twice!

59
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,667
- Okay, do you think you
could make witty remarks

60
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:33,300
all the way through
this week's movie?

61
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:35,133
- Yes, oh yes, oh
yes, oh yes, oh yes!

62
00:02:35,167 --> 00:02:36,633
Sisters are doing
it for themselves.

63
00:02:36,667 --> 00:02:38,000
- You're on, Gypsy!

64
00:02:38,033 --> 00:02:40,567
- Oh, thank you, Mr.
Robinson, you won't be sorry!

65
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,200
- I can't believe it.
- Well, gotta go!

66
00:02:42,233 --> 00:02:43,967
Don't start the
movie without me!

67
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,967
- Ixnay on the Ypsyjay!

68
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,767
- Come on, you
guys, take it easy.

69
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,400
You know, don't be
too hard on Gypsy,

70
00:02:49,433 --> 00:02:51,100
we might have a
good time in there.

71
00:02:51,133 --> 00:02:53,567
- Joel, you should've
stopped at two, Joel.

72
00:02:54,433 --> 00:02:57,000
(upbeat music)

73
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,633
♪ Everyone's going to a movie ♪

74
00:03:02,667 --> 00:03:05,200
- I don't know, Joel, I
still don't think it's

75
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:07,500
a very good idea to have
Gypsy watch the movie with us.

76
00:03:07,533 --> 00:03:09,800
- Yeah, I mean, she's a fun gal,

77
00:03:09,833 --> 00:03:12,000
she's got her own groove,
but to be quite frank,

78
00:03:12,033 --> 00:03:14,267
I just don't think she's
down with the street.

79
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:15,700
- Well, I guess we'll find out.

80
00:03:15,733 --> 00:03:18,533
Oops, looks like the
glimmer twins are calling.

81
00:03:18,567 --> 00:03:22,167
- Good idea, Joel, get
Gypsy in on the fun.

82
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,067
(laughing)
(hammering)

83
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:26,433
Well, what I wanted
to say, Frank!

84
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:31,567
Anyway, Joel, I've been on
retreat most of this week.

85
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:34,200
Three days of silence,

86
00:03:34,233 --> 00:03:37,100
prayer and simple food,

87
00:03:37,133 --> 00:03:39,767
and I've left the invention
exchange up to Frank.

88
00:03:40,767 --> 00:03:44,000
Yes, learning to relax,

89
00:03:44,033 --> 00:03:45,933
learning to trust.

90
00:03:45,967 --> 00:03:48,167
Let's see what he's
come up with, hmm?

91
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,533
Frank?

92
00:03:49,567 --> 00:03:51,000
- Well, thank you.

93
00:03:51,033 --> 00:03:53,100
As you all might remember,
Doctor Forrester and I

94
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:55,233
run a pretty hot
little daycare business

95
00:03:55,267 --> 00:03:56,967
down here in Deep 13.

96
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,467
Doctor F handles
the business side

97
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:02,033
so I know all about
learning to trust.

98
00:04:02,067 --> 00:04:03,467
(chuckling)

99
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:07,067
Whereas I handle the actually,
the actual hands-on work

100
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:09,133
of working with the
toddlers down here,

101
00:04:09,167 --> 00:04:12,033
and yet I'm still stuck
doing all the lawn work.

102
00:04:12,067 --> 00:04:15,767
Well, that's why I've
invented Lawn Baby.

103
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:19,067
Now our lawn can still have
that silken suburban sheen,

104
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:21,133
at the same time, I
can take little baby

105
00:04:21,167 --> 00:04:22,633
for a leisurely stroll.

106
00:04:22,667 --> 00:04:25,200
Wanna hand me that?
- Here you go, Frank.

107
00:04:25,233 --> 00:04:26,433
(crying)

108
00:04:26,467 --> 00:04:27,500
Frank!

109
00:04:27,533 --> 00:04:29,133
You could've hurt baby Melvin!

110
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:32,500
Well, Joel, as you
can see, it's okay,

111
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:36,167
you can see this one may not
fly without a little more work.

112
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:37,700
So much for trusting.
(crying)

113
00:04:37,733 --> 00:04:38,967
Oh, that's okay.

114
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,533
Why don't you go on with
your invention exchange?

115
00:04:41,567 --> 00:04:43,900
- What a coincidence, you know,
we've also been getting into

116
00:04:43,933 --> 00:04:47,000
the nesting instinct up here
on the Satellite of Love.

117
00:04:47,033 --> 00:04:49,300
You know, it's becoming
popular for young parents

118
00:04:49,333 --> 00:04:51,767
to begin molding and
shaping their children

119
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,767
from a very early age.

120
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,900
- Why, Joel, you're radiant!

121
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:57,667
- You're more
beautiful than ever.

122
00:04:57,700 --> 00:04:58,900
- Thanks, you guys.

123
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:00,533
And we thought it would
be a really neat idea

124
00:05:00,567 --> 00:05:03,367
for prenatal kids to get in on
some of the really cool music

125
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,467
that's going on right
now and also cash in

126
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:08,567
on some of those self
motivational tapes.

127
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,833
Enter the Wombmate.

128
00:05:10,867 --> 00:05:12,967
You've got these headphones
that go over your stomach

129
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,500
like this and then
you play a tape.

130
00:05:15,533 --> 00:05:18,700
Say you want the leader
of a future generation?

131
00:05:18,733 --> 00:05:22,133
Play the theme music from
2001: A Space Odyssey,

132
00:05:22,167 --> 00:05:23,500
"Thus Spoke Zarathustra."

133
00:05:24,933 --> 00:05:27,333
- And if you want an infant
who can sell, sell, sell,

134
00:05:27,367 --> 00:05:30,400
just pop in Brian Tracy's,
"Psychology of Achievement."

135
00:05:30,433 --> 00:05:32,400
- You know, everyone
has abandonment issues.

136
00:05:32,433 --> 00:05:33,900
- Sure.

137
00:05:33,933 --> 00:05:35,333
- So play John Bradshaw's,
"Healing the Child Within,"

138
00:05:35,367 --> 00:05:37,933
for you child within
your child within.

139
00:05:37,967 --> 00:05:39,367
Hey, what's playing now, Joel?

140
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,300
- Oh, hmm, I don't
know, let me check.

141
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,767
It's Nazareth's "Hair
of the Dog" album.

142
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,967
- Oh, that's mine, how'd
that get in there anyway?

143
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,400
- I don't know, but I'm
sure glad I'm not pregnant.

144
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:52,267
- You're not, are you?
- No, of course not, silly.

145
00:05:53,133 --> 00:05:55,267
What do you think, sirs?

146
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:57,067
- I'm having a little
problem hearing.

147
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:59,467
(crying)

148
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:02,000
I'm having a little
trouble hearing you.

149
00:06:02,033 --> 00:06:04,900
Anyway, your experiment
this week is,

150
00:06:04,933 --> 00:06:09,100
sad to say, the last
of the Hercules movies.

151
00:06:09,133 --> 00:06:11,333
I can't even tell you the name
of the stiff that plays him

152
00:06:11,367 --> 00:06:12,267
this time out.

153
00:06:13,667 --> 00:06:16,367
Anyway, I've gotta go help
Frank with his little problem.

154
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:18,000
Why don't you go on ahead?

155
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:23,767
(alarm blaring)
(yelling)

156
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,633
(doors whooshing)

157
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,000
- [Gypsy] Movie's starting!

158
00:06:32,033 --> 00:06:35,500
Come on, you guys,
Joel, Crow, Servo!

159
00:06:35,533 --> 00:06:36,467
- [Joel] Hi, Gypsy.

160
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,700
- [Gypsy] Hercules
and the Captive Women,

161
00:06:39,733 --> 00:06:41,567
well this sounds really fun.

162
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,500
- [Crow] Oh, Gypsy,
you are so naive.

163
00:06:43,533 --> 00:06:46,233
- [Tom] Guys, I read
hieroglyphs, this
says that one time

164
00:06:46,267 --> 00:06:48,067
this big lobster came
and attacked a lady

165
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:49,467
but Mr. Ed saved her.
(chuckling)

166
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:52,533
- Really?
- I think he's kidding, Gypsy.

167
00:06:52,567 --> 00:06:54,033
- [Gypsy] Oh.

168
00:06:54,067 --> 00:06:55,367
- [Tom] Man, I knew it,
Gypsy can't hang with us,

169
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:56,967
she's just isn't
down with the street!

170
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,033
- [Joel] Oh, come on, I
think she's doing fine.

171
00:06:59,067 --> 00:07:00,467
- [Crow] Oh,
where's the sarcasm?

172
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,067
Where's the biting
acerbic commentary?

173
00:07:02,100 --> 00:07:03,600
Where's the scimitar wit?

174
00:07:03,633 --> 00:07:05,067
- Rapier, rapier.
- Yeah, whatever.

175
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:06,467
Come on, Gypsy, let's have it!

176
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:07,767
- Come on.
- Um, okay.

177
00:07:09,067 --> 00:07:11,867
Look at that dumb
name, that's so stupid!

178
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:13,567
- [Crow] Oh brother!

179
00:07:15,333 --> 00:07:18,033
- [Tom] Hey, General Music
Company, nothin' specific.

180
00:07:18,067 --> 00:07:19,933
Slow or fast, that's
about all we have.

181
00:07:19,967 --> 00:07:21,800
(chuckling)

182
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:26,833
(awe-inspiring music)
(vocalizing)

183
00:07:27,933 --> 00:07:29,500
- [Joel] Hey, look,
a chili pizza.

184
00:07:29,533 --> 00:07:30,967
Who's hungry for chili pizza?

185
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,133
- [Gypsy] I am, that
sounds delicious.

186
00:07:33,167 --> 00:07:35,333
- [Tom] Gypsy, I weep for you.

187
00:07:35,367 --> 00:07:38,533
(awe-inspiring music)

188
00:07:38,567 --> 00:07:39,900
Cottafani candy.

189
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,167
- Bonanza!
- This is ancient Greece.

190
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:47,433
- [Tom] And if that map
burns, it'll be a Greece fire.

191
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:48,933
(chuckling)
- Good one.

192
00:07:50,233 --> 00:07:52,400
- [Narrator] The
King of Thebes was--

193
00:07:52,433 --> 00:07:55,267
- [Joel] Was what,
what happened to him?

194
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:57,133
- [Tom] Oh forget it,
just enjoy, friends.

195
00:07:57,167 --> 00:07:58,633
- [Narrator] Hercules
and his son Hylas

196
00:07:58,667 --> 00:08:00,567
were loyal to this brave ruler.

197
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:02,633
- I'm the King of Thebes!

198
00:08:03,767 --> 00:08:05,433
- [Gypsy] Hey,
hey, stop fighting,

199
00:08:05,467 --> 00:08:07,667
everybody stop fighting!
- It's okay, Gypsy,

200
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:08,600
it's just a movie.

201
00:08:10,067 --> 00:08:12,767
- [Crow] The service here is
great, even during a fight!

202
00:08:14,233 --> 00:08:16,100
- [Narrator] Good-natured
brawling was a necessity.

203
00:08:16,133 --> 00:08:17,533
- [Crow] Good natured?

204
00:08:17,567 --> 00:08:19,600
- [Narrator] To keep the
young warriors fit and strong.

205
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:21,833
The wars were always present.

206
00:08:21,867 --> 00:08:23,667
(yelling)

207
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:25,567
- [Tom] Boy, it's busier
in here than usual.

208
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:28,133
- [Crow] I hope
that's not Hercules.

209
00:08:28,167 --> 00:08:29,633
Oh no, it is!

210
00:08:29,667 --> 00:08:30,867
- [Hercules] That's
enough now, boys.

211
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,600
- [Tom] You got a
phone I can use?

212
00:08:34,033 --> 00:08:35,533
- Come on.
- Oh they're bathing together,

213
00:08:35,567 --> 00:08:37,933
that's weird.
- Not in Greece it isn't.

214
00:08:39,667 --> 00:08:41,667
- [Gypsy] Oh, they've
got a fun friend!

215
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:43,467
- [Crow] And we've got
a junior buffalo shot.

216
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,833
(chuckling)

217
00:08:46,867 --> 00:08:49,200
(vocalizing)

218
00:08:49,233 --> 00:08:50,433
- [Timoteo] You too!

219
00:08:50,467 --> 00:08:52,000
- [Narrator] History
tells us of the war--

220
00:08:52,033 --> 00:08:53,467
- [Joel] And now
I'm going to too.

221
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:55,767
- [Narrator] Tell us of an
era when the unforeseen perils

222
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:59,200
of the mystical unknown
were always lurking.

223
00:09:00,467 --> 00:09:02,933
This is one of those legends.

224
00:09:02,967 --> 00:09:04,600
(wind blowing)

225
00:09:04,633 --> 00:09:07,533
- [Gypsy] Hey, get this, they're
steam cleaning the horses!

226
00:09:07,567 --> 00:09:09,167
- All right, good one!
- Hey!

227
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,467
- You've got it.
- Yeah.

228
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,700
- Look there, the sun!

229
00:09:12,733 --> 00:09:14,767
- [Tom] Yeah, what's
it doing up there?

230
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:17,433
(ominous music)

231
00:09:17,467 --> 00:09:20,200
- [Man] Stop, stop
where are you going?

232
00:09:20,233 --> 00:09:23,433
All Greece is bleeding,
pity our poor country!

233
00:09:23,467 --> 00:09:24,900
Flee for your lives!

234
00:09:24,933 --> 00:09:27,033
- What are you trying to
say, where do you come from?

235
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:28,567
- [Crow] Who's your daddy?

236
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,067
- [Man] Not from wounds, but
is falling from the heavens

237
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:32,267
with flames and poisonous
serpents, monstrous powers--

238
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:34,100
- [Joel] Sounds pretty bad.

239
00:09:34,133 --> 00:09:36,400
- [Man] In all our cities,
the people are fleeing before

240
00:09:36,433 --> 00:09:39,067
the deadly shadow which is
bringing night without end!

241
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:41,967
Can't you see the rain
of blood and fire?

242
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,133
- He's long winded.
- Yeah.

243
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:45,500
- The cities of Greece.
- Hermie.

244
00:09:45,533 --> 00:09:47,333
- From the heavens!
- Pink and red.

245
00:09:47,367 --> 00:09:48,667
- From the heavens!
- That's great,

246
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:50,800
really good audition
piece, thank you.

247
00:09:50,833 --> 00:09:52,333
- [Crow] Very nice, very nice.

248
00:09:52,367 --> 00:09:54,433
(ominous music)

249
00:09:54,467 --> 00:09:57,267
- [Tom] It's like
roller bubbles.

250
00:09:57,300 --> 00:09:58,700
That must be that
Moses character

251
00:09:58,733 --> 00:10:01,833
I've heard him talk
about so much lately.

252
00:10:01,867 --> 00:10:02,933
- [Joel] Mmm.

253
00:10:07,033 --> 00:10:09,567
- [Crow] He's not
heavy, he's my brother.

254
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:12,267
(ominous music)

255
00:10:13,233 --> 00:10:15,633
- [Tom] Ooh, sundogs.

256
00:10:15,667 --> 00:10:17,333
- Where did he go to,
what did he leave?

257
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:20,067
- I don't know, it must be
a sign from the heavens.

258
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,300
Only the prophet Tiresias
can tell us what it means.

259
00:10:22,333 --> 00:10:23,800
- He's in Thebes, come on.

260
00:10:23,833 --> 00:10:25,467
- [Joel] Whack today,
we weren't supposed

261
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:27,267
to take the brown acid.

262
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:28,267
- [Gypsy] I don't get it.

263
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:29,867
- [Tom] Neither do we, Gypsy.

264
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:32,567
(vocalizing)

265
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:37,600
♪ How do you solve a
problem like Maria ♪

266
00:10:39,067 --> 00:10:40,167
- [Crow] I think it's a
take back the night march.

267
00:10:41,367 --> 00:10:43,200
- [Joel] I think
we're being followed.

268
00:10:43,233 --> 00:10:44,033
Just act natural.

269
00:10:47,033 --> 00:10:49,300
- [Tom] Hope he
can make that hill.

270
00:10:49,333 --> 00:10:50,567
(screeching)

271
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:51,900
- [Tiresias] The
gods have spoken.

272
00:10:51,933 --> 00:10:54,233
- [Tom] But I couldn't
understand them.

273
00:10:54,267 --> 00:10:58,033
- With lightning, with the
winds they have spoken.

274
00:10:58,067 --> 00:11:00,900
But not by menacing
or by punishing

275
00:11:00,933 --> 00:11:04,867
but through their life-giving
powers they have spoken.

276
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:05,733
- What have they
said, oh wise one?

277
00:11:07,067 --> 00:11:08,300
- [Crow] They said,
"Will the owner of a

278
00:11:08,333 --> 00:11:10,667
"white Toyota Camry please--"
- Who can say?

279
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:14,233
A peril hangs over all our land.

280
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,867
A peril from afar.

281
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:21,400
- [Joel] In fact, apparel
is half off this week.

282
00:11:21,433 --> 00:11:23,133
- Who would dare
attack the Greeks?

283
00:11:23,167 --> 00:11:24,533
- Evil is upon us.

284
00:11:25,533 --> 00:11:27,933
Forces of unbelievable horror.

285
00:11:27,967 --> 00:11:30,200
- Horror.
- To the people.

286
00:11:30,233 --> 00:11:33,833
- Through the straights from
which no vessel has returned.

287
00:11:35,733 --> 00:11:36,867
- [Crow] Over here.

288
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:38,933
- [Tiresias] Across
unknown seas.

289
00:11:38,967 --> 00:11:40,967
- [Gypsy] You guys,
you know, this movie

290
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,833
isn't really that good.
- Yeah.

291
00:11:42,867 --> 00:11:43,833
- [Tom] Yes.

292
00:11:43,867 --> 00:11:45,033
Right, that's true.

293
00:11:46,667 --> 00:11:47,867
That's great, gramps.

294
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:49,233
Start the car,
I'll be right out.

295
00:11:49,267 --> 00:11:52,000
- [Gypsy] Um, you
guys, I just remembered

296
00:11:52,033 --> 00:11:54,100
I've got a billion things to do.

297
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:55,600
- [Joel] What, you
can't leave now,

298
00:11:55,633 --> 00:11:57,833
you wanted to sit through
the whole experiment.

299
00:11:57,867 --> 00:12:01,967
- [Gypsy] But, that
was before I knew,

300
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
and then there
were these things.

301
00:12:04,033 --> 00:12:05,767
And now I have to go do them.

302
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:07,267
- [Crow] Well, if you
can't stand the heat.

303
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:09,600
- [Joel] That's okay, Gypsy,
run along, that's really fine.

304
00:12:09,633 --> 00:12:11,067
- [Tom] Go on.

305
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:13,533
- The city councilors to ever
manage to reach an accord.

306
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:16,267
- Thanks to the guards I
alone commanded my kingdom.

307
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:17,767
Androcles is right, we should--

308
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,400
- [Joel] She did her best,
I don't want you guys--

309
00:12:19,433 --> 00:12:21,033
- [Crow] Shh, Joel,
watch the movie!

310
00:12:21,067 --> 00:12:23,833
- [Joel] Please,
it's a bad movie.

311
00:12:23,867 --> 00:12:25,233
- [Crow] I'll just sit.

312
00:12:25,267 --> 00:12:28,267
(laughing)

313
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:29,633
- [Tom] Shut up, it's not funny.

314
00:12:29,667 --> 00:12:31,133
- Better to divide
ourselves, one post attacks

315
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:33,233
the other defends.

316
00:12:33,267 --> 00:12:34,867
- Dear brothers, we didn't
come here to bring up

317
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:36,467
the things which divide us.

318
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:39,433
We must unite against the
enemy that menaces us.

319
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:41,533
Would you perhaps prefer
that we wait here helplessly

320
00:12:41,567 --> 00:12:43,933
for the moment when the
enemy will decide to attack,

321
00:12:43,967 --> 00:12:45,967
to destroy all of our cities?

322
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,300
- [Joel] He's got
Earl Campbell thighs.

323
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:49,533
- My soldiers are invincible

324
00:12:49,567 --> 00:12:52,400
and my navy big enough
to transport them.

325
00:12:52,433 --> 00:12:55,633
(gasping)
(stammering)

326
00:12:55,667 --> 00:12:57,033
- [Crow] Return to my seat.

327
00:12:58,500 --> 00:13:00,867
- Watch, Androcles, look
at the outlines of Greece

328
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:03,600
over on the map, and within
the confines of my own land.

329
00:13:03,633 --> 00:13:05,433
I swear by all the gods--
- Gimme that.

330
00:13:05,467 --> 00:13:06,867
- That no enemy will ever pass.

331
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:08,567
- Look out, he's drunk!
- Duck!

332
00:13:09,467 --> 00:13:11,967
(boinging)

333
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,733
- Doesn't impress me.
- Look here!

334
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:16,667
(boinging)

335
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:17,867
(laughing)

336
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:19,133
- If you think
I'd be impressed--

337
00:13:19,167 --> 00:13:21,467
- [Joel] Ah, excuse
me, you're on fire.

338
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:23,167
(blowing)

339
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:25,867
- Even a king can
court misfortune if
he's too intriguing.

340
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:27,500
- [Crow] Hey, Dr. Zira!

341
00:13:27,533 --> 00:13:28,767
- The tribute money
from the last war

342
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,267
is still waiting to be paid.

343
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:32,333
- If you think to fill
your coffers with my gold

344
00:13:32,367 --> 00:13:34,367
because we're now
forced to be allies...

345
00:13:35,433 --> 00:13:37,133
No!
- Okay, yes!

346
00:13:37,167 --> 00:13:38,567
I changed my mind.

347
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:41,000
- I must go alone.
- They lost me.

348
00:13:41,033 --> 00:13:42,933
Way back there.
- Abandoning my kingdom

349
00:13:42,967 --> 00:13:44,833
to defend all of yours?

350
00:13:44,867 --> 00:13:46,067
- Oh!
- Look at that guy!

351
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:48,833
- See to it that nobody
sits upon your throne

352
00:13:48,867 --> 00:13:51,200
during your absence.
(yelling)

353
00:13:51,233 --> 00:13:52,967
- [Crow] Yuck, do you mind?

354
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:56,000
- [Tom] I think it would
go something like this.

355
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:59,833
- [Joel] If you don't
mind, I kinda need to do

356
00:13:59,867 --> 00:14:01,467
some squats right now.

357
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,000
- [Crow] Take this
out to the garage.

358
00:14:03,033 --> 00:14:04,167
Wonder what his max is?

359
00:14:07,433 --> 00:14:08,533
- Your throne shall be rebuilt

360
00:14:08,567 --> 00:14:10,000
the day you return, Androcles.

361
00:14:10,033 --> 00:14:11,433
- [Tom] Uh, thanks, I think.

362
00:14:11,467 --> 00:14:13,967
- What a waste of a fine throne.

363
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,100
It was carved especially
for me in Tyros.

364
00:14:16,133 --> 00:14:17,467
- [Crow] Now it's garbage.

365
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:19,100
- We shall sculpt one
far more beautiful

366
00:14:19,133 --> 00:14:20,867
to celebrate your homecoming.

367
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,267
- [Tom] But I can't go
to homecoming with you.

368
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:25,900
(upbeat music)

369
00:14:29,167 --> 00:14:30,800
(adventurous music)

370
00:14:30,833 --> 00:14:32,667
It's a Carnival cruise ship.

371
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:39,967
(gentle instrumental music)

372
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,500
(groaning)

373
00:14:41,533 --> 00:14:44,833
- [Crow] I'm almost done,
hey, bring me a magazine.

374
00:14:44,867 --> 00:14:46,067
- [Joel] You know what, Tony?

375
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:47,867
If we all work together
we could beat Harvard!

376
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,033
- Do you think
he'll be very mad?

377
00:14:51,067 --> 00:14:52,800
- Difficult to say
before he wakes up.

378
00:14:52,833 --> 00:14:55,133
No matter, we're
miles from shore.

379
00:14:55,167 --> 00:14:58,167
- When papa finds out I put a
sleeping powder in his wine...

380
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,867
- Hey, he's coming around.

381
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:01,800
- You take over, if he
finds out that I'm here

382
00:15:01,833 --> 00:15:03,000
on board we're all done for!

383
00:15:03,033 --> 00:15:04,500
- [Tom] Well if he finds
out you dressed him

384
00:15:04,533 --> 00:15:07,400
in a mini skirt you'll be
in even bigger trouble.

385
00:15:07,433 --> 00:15:08,433
- [Timoteo] Wait,
I'll come with ya!

386
00:15:08,467 --> 00:15:09,700
- No, you stay here.

387
00:15:10,867 --> 00:15:13,233
- [Crow] Oh, sure, boss
around the little guy.

388
00:15:16,167 --> 00:15:18,200
(vocalizing)

389
00:15:18,233 --> 00:15:19,200
- [Joel] Down the hatch.

390
00:15:19,233 --> 00:15:20,967
Ooh, I didn't see that.

391
00:15:23,567 --> 00:15:25,533
(groaning)

392
00:15:25,567 --> 00:15:27,967
- [Crow] Whoa, did I
toss a throne last night?

393
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:31,967
- [Joel] Oh, I must've
overslept, Hercules style.

394
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:37,167
- [Tom] Anybody know where
to get breakfast around here?

395
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:39,200
(chewing)
(burping)

396
00:15:39,233 --> 00:15:40,900
- [Joel] Why you son of a...

397
00:15:40,933 --> 00:15:43,067
(chuckling)

398
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:45,267
- Lovely day, isn't it?
- Yep.

399
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:46,400
(chuckling nervously)

400
00:15:46,433 --> 00:15:47,867
- [Crow] Don't hurt me.

401
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:49,167
- [Tom] That's nice, huh?

402
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,767
- How long have we been at sea?

403
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:54,967
- Since sun up.

404
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,067
- [Tom] Oh, sun up,
good, yes, that's nice.

405
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:00,267
I wanna go home, I wanna
go home to the farm,

406
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:02,067
I wanna go home!
- Where's your fleet?

407
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:07,000
- At the bottom of my leg.
- Well...

408
00:16:07,033 --> 00:16:09,567
- And where are your warriors?

409
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:12,000
- [Joel] I ate 'em?

410
00:16:12,033 --> 00:16:14,567
- It's because of that
I brought you with us.

411
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:16,600
- I understand, I understand.

412
00:16:16,633 --> 00:16:19,100
- [Tom] I'm a rational
man, I'm a rational man.

413
00:16:19,133 --> 00:16:22,700
- And is this your crew?
- They're my little brother's

414
00:16:22,733 --> 00:16:24,633
friends, there's
really nothing much.

415
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:28,633
- [Crow] All right, I love
it, we're gonna have fun.

416
00:16:28,667 --> 00:16:31,167
- Fine company.
- It's the best I could find.

417
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:36,333
- But I thought you
were the King of Thebes.

418
00:16:36,367 --> 00:16:37,800
(scoffing)
- I wish!

419
00:16:37,833 --> 00:16:39,367
- I fought against the
soothsayers, the senators,

420
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:41,000
the commanders of the army.

421
00:16:41,033 --> 00:16:42,833
Aren't you always saying
that democracy is--

422
00:16:42,867 --> 00:16:44,300
- Never mind, never mind.

423
00:16:44,333 --> 00:16:47,000
Any way, I was right to
smash the throne, wasn't I?

424
00:16:47,033 --> 00:16:49,167
- [Joel] Oh, lay that one on me.

425
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:50,033
- [Tom] Ooh!

426
00:16:50,867 --> 00:16:51,700
- Now,

427
00:16:52,933 --> 00:16:55,267
how do you intend
to beat the enemy?

428
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:56,533
(yelling)

429
00:16:56,567 --> 00:16:58,733
Oh, I forgot.
- Hey, Hercules, put him down!

430
00:16:58,767 --> 00:17:00,500
- We've got Timoteo.

431
00:17:00,533 --> 00:17:01,633
- No need for irony.

432
00:17:03,033 --> 00:17:04,833
An enemy we've never seen
is twice as powerful.

433
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,767
We now have to find
out who this enemy is.

434
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,200
- [Joel] All done?

435
00:17:09,233 --> 00:17:10,400
- [Androcles] From what
unknown land he threatens us.

436
00:17:10,433 --> 00:17:11,633
How strong he is.
- Yeah, sure.

437
00:17:11,667 --> 00:17:12,900
- How great are his armies?
(groaning)

438
00:17:12,933 --> 00:17:15,100
From where does he
intend to attack us?

439
00:17:15,133 --> 00:17:15,933
- [Tom] Look, wake
me up when you get

440
00:17:15,967 --> 00:17:17,733
to the plot point, okay?

441
00:17:19,067 --> 00:17:19,967
Good night.

442
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,667
- Hercules, what are you doing?

443
00:17:22,533 --> 00:17:23,367
- I'm sleepy.

444
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,400
- Aw, that's our Herc!
(vocalizing)

445
00:17:29,433 --> 00:17:31,633
That's, oh that funny,
cumbersome clown.

446
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:34,767
- I'd prefer for
him to hit somebody.

447
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:37,700
- [Crow] Well, whatever tugs
at your bobber, little fella.

448
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:39,700
- [Joel] Steve Austin.

449
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:44,000
- [Tom] Meanwhile, in
the very same scene...

450
00:17:45,067 --> 00:17:47,500
(vocalizing)

451
00:17:48,933 --> 00:17:50,800
- [Crow] Hey, come back
here with my dinner roll!

452
00:17:50,833 --> 00:17:51,933
- [Tom] You weren't
gonna eat it anyway!

453
00:17:51,967 --> 00:17:53,367
- I was too!
- I seem to remember

454
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:56,133
my fruit cup being missing.
- You took my brownie

455
00:17:56,167 --> 00:17:57,600
the other day!
- I didn't take your brownie.

456
00:17:57,633 --> 00:17:58,800
- [Tom] I buttered it,
you didn't even butter it!

457
00:17:58,833 --> 00:18:01,133
- [Joel] Push him over,
push him overboard.

458
00:18:01,167 --> 00:18:03,067
- [Tom] Give you another
dinner roll some other time.

459
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:04,433
No, I'm afraid it's mine.

460
00:18:06,767 --> 00:18:07,600
Dinner roll.

461
00:18:08,667 --> 00:18:09,867
- Yeah?
- Dinner roll you.

462
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:11,400
Hey, who left the
rudder on land?

463
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:14,667
- [Tom] Oh jeez, I got a
backup on table 10 and,

464
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:15,967
oh, good morning, sir.

465
00:18:17,167 --> 00:18:19,533
Frosted Lucky Charms, sir.
- Wake up!

466
00:18:19,567 --> 00:18:20,767
I brought some food.
(groaning)

467
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:23,067
- [Crow] I went home with you?

468
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:24,467
- Oh, it's impossible.

469
00:18:25,633 --> 00:18:27,833
I've hid down here in
this hole six long days.

470
00:18:28,967 --> 00:18:30,467
I've gotten seasick
in the bargain.

471
00:18:31,533 --> 00:18:32,333
I'm going up.

472
00:18:32,367 --> 00:18:33,767
- No!
- No you don't!

473
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:35,333
- [Tom] Buffalo shot
to yourself there!

474
00:18:35,367 --> 00:18:37,433
- We're lost if Hercules
finds you on board.

475
00:18:37,467 --> 00:18:38,967
The only thing he's been
asking all these days

476
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,067
is whether you're at
home safe and sound.

477
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:43,967
- Did you tell him I was?
- Don't be silly.

478
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:47,467
- What else did he say?
- Nothing, mostly he sleeps.

479
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:49,300
When he doesn't sleep he fishes.

480
00:18:49,333 --> 00:18:52,500
- Fishes?
- You know, line, hook, worm?

481
00:18:52,533 --> 00:18:53,367
- None.

482
00:18:55,233 --> 00:18:57,300
- [Crow] Good night
now, that's our time.

483
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:00,200
- [Tom] Join us in the world
of snails and adventure

484
00:19:00,233 --> 00:19:04,700
as we board the Golden Hind.
(adventurous music)

485
00:19:04,733 --> 00:19:07,033
- [Joel] Oh great,
a Marmaduke ship.

486
00:19:07,067 --> 00:19:09,233
(barking)

487
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,067
- [Tom] Maybe if the
pulled up the anchor

488
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:15,200
the plot would move a little.

489
00:19:15,233 --> 00:19:18,700
- [Crow] Oh Harry, taking
pictures of nothing again?

490
00:19:18,733 --> 00:19:21,667
(gentle instrumental music)

491
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,900
- [Tom] Oh dear lord,
the canary exploded!

492
00:19:23,933 --> 00:19:25,033
- Oh no!
- So sad.

493
00:19:25,067 --> 00:19:27,867
- Hercules is sleeping.
- Oh, big news.

494
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:28,800
- Won't bother us.

495
00:19:32,900 --> 00:19:35,100
- [Joel] That is a
juicy cut of beef.

496
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:38,000
So juicy and oily and good.

497
00:19:38,033 --> 00:19:41,133
- [Crow] Let's see how Mr.
Rockford does without any water.

498
00:19:43,367 --> 00:19:46,233
- [Tom] Can God himself
make a plot so complicated

499
00:19:46,267 --> 00:19:48,367
that even he can't
comprehend it?

500
00:19:50,467 --> 00:19:52,833
- [Joel] Gee Davy...

501
00:19:52,867 --> 00:19:55,433
(upbeat music)

502
00:19:57,567 --> 00:19:58,967
- [Crow] That's the Blue Lagoon.

503
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,467
- [Tom] No, no, I think
it's James A. Michener's

504
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:03,433
Adventures in Paradise.

505
00:20:07,567 --> 00:20:08,967
- [Soldier] Move along,
don't be so slow!

506
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,833
- [Joel] Okay, now
stay with the tour,

507
00:20:10,867 --> 00:20:13,667
over here is where they
filmed Hercs-a-Poppin

508
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:16,633
and Hercules 69 and
of course Grease 2.

509
00:20:16,667 --> 00:20:17,500
♪ Shake shake shake ♪

510
00:20:17,533 --> 00:20:18,467
♪ Shake shake shake ♪

511
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:19,400
♪ Shake your booty ♪

512
00:20:19,433 --> 00:20:20,800
- [Crow] Come on, everybody.

513
00:20:21,967 --> 00:20:23,467
- [Joel] Wonder
what they wanted?

514
00:20:25,067 --> 00:20:27,533
- [Crow] Say, now
that is a micro mini.

515
00:20:27,567 --> 00:20:28,900
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

516
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,200
Seen my pants?

517
00:20:32,233 --> 00:20:34,500
(rustling)

518
00:20:36,167 --> 00:20:37,100
- [Androcles] Hey.

519
00:20:37,133 --> 00:20:38,067
- [Crow] Thanks for kicking me.

520
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:39,367
- That water can't be far off.

521
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:41,133
- [Joel] Ah, it's
right behind you.

522
00:20:41,167 --> 00:20:42,600
- We should leave

523
00:20:42,633 --> 00:20:43,867
before the sun goes down.
- Right over there.

524
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:46,133
- [Tom] You are gonna
fry and age prematurely.

525
00:20:47,967 --> 00:20:48,767
- Look yonder.

526
00:20:50,233 --> 00:20:52,100
There in that direction
is the mysterious country.

527
00:20:52,133 --> 00:20:53,767
If we can find it with
the aid of the gods

528
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:56,300
we can confront the
danger that's menacing us.

529
00:20:56,333 --> 00:20:58,533
- What makes you so sure
the gods will help us?

530
00:20:58,567 --> 00:21:00,400
- [Crow] Chew on that.

531
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:04,533
- I'll go and look
for the men now,

532
00:21:04,567 --> 00:21:06,767
I can't believe that rats
gnawed those water bags.

533
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:08,567
Human rats with swords, maybe.

534
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:11,433
Certainly not the best of men
for an enterprise like this.

535
00:21:11,467 --> 00:21:12,533
- [Tom] Teenagers!

536
00:21:14,633 --> 00:21:16,067
- Sleep well, don't
trouble yourself,

537
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:18,100
I'll wake you just
before we go aboard.

538
00:21:18,133 --> 00:21:19,700
- Go ahead, honey.
- Yeah.

539
00:21:19,733 --> 00:21:22,467
- [Tom] Hercules, sleeping
all the time, buffalo shots,

540
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:23,933
I don't need this.

541
00:21:23,967 --> 00:21:25,833
Perseus, now there's
a man I could,

542
00:21:25,867 --> 00:21:27,600
(muttering)
tosses Hercules.

543
00:21:30,833 --> 00:21:34,000
- [Crow] A planet where
apes evolved from man?

544
00:21:34,033 --> 00:21:37,133
(ominous music)

545
00:21:37,167 --> 00:21:38,500
- [Joel] Man Dance '92.

546
00:21:40,533 --> 00:21:42,267
- Help!
- It's clop clop for men.

547
00:21:43,433 --> 00:21:44,967
A round table when?

548
00:21:46,467 --> 00:21:48,667
- [Crow] Come on, everybody,
we're beatin' up on stinky!

549
00:21:50,900 --> 00:21:53,100
(vocalizing)

550
00:21:53,133 --> 00:21:55,200
- [Joel] Hey, do you guys
remember why we're doing this?

551
00:21:55,233 --> 00:21:56,533
- [Tom] No, I'm in the film

552
00:21:56,567 --> 00:21:58,600
and I don't even
know what's going on.

553
00:21:58,633 --> 00:21:59,567
- [Crow] Well let's
get out of here

554
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:01,033
or our careers are done for!

555
00:22:04,433 --> 00:22:06,133
- They're on the shore
but you stay below.

556
00:22:06,167 --> 00:22:08,067
- [Hylas] Just let
me see the sky.

557
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:09,700
- You think doing
that's all just--

558
00:22:09,733 --> 00:22:11,333
- [Crow] I have my
rights, I have my rights,

559
00:22:11,367 --> 00:22:13,967
it was baby Callahan!
(crying)

560
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,300
- [Hylas] No, no, I'm coming up.

561
00:22:15,333 --> 00:22:16,767
- Wait, the soldiers
are coming back!

562
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:19,600
- [Joel] Oh, I didn't
need those fingers anyway!

563
00:22:24,067 --> 00:22:26,633
(yelling)

564
00:22:26,667 --> 00:22:29,500
(doors whooshing)

565
00:22:34,533 --> 00:22:35,867
- Joel, do you think
there's such a thing

566
00:22:35,900 --> 00:22:37,100
as good-natured brawling?

567
00:22:37,133 --> 00:22:38,500
- Oh, I never really
thought about it,

568
00:22:38,533 --> 00:22:39,600
sometimes when you see--
(yelling)

569
00:22:39,633 --> 00:22:42,833
Oh, why you dirty...
(yelling)

570
00:22:42,867 --> 00:22:44,800
- I would not do
that if I were you!

571
00:22:44,833 --> 00:22:46,433
(yelling)

572
00:22:46,467 --> 00:22:49,400
- That's it, out you pixies go
to the door, out the window!

573
00:22:49,433 --> 00:22:51,900
- Oh yeah, well I'm gonna mop
the barroom floor with you!

574
00:22:51,933 --> 00:22:54,067
(yelling)

575
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:57,533
- What in tarnation?

576
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:02,867
(yelling)
(growling)

577
00:23:05,867 --> 00:23:07,000
- Huh?

578
00:23:07,033 --> 00:23:09,200
(yelling)

579
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:12,733
(groaning)

580
00:23:17,967 --> 00:23:20,733
He's cracking up, Frank,
we've finally done it!

581
00:23:22,633 --> 00:23:23,767
- Ew.

582
00:23:23,800 --> 00:23:25,333
(chuckling)
- Oh that was fun.

583
00:23:25,367 --> 00:23:27,200
Now what was your
question again?

584
00:23:27,233 --> 00:23:28,900
I'm kidding, of course.

585
00:23:28,933 --> 00:23:32,967
Yes there is such a thing
as good-natured brawling.

586
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,800
- [All] We'll be right back.

587
00:23:34,833 --> 00:23:37,667
- I want Joe Frazier,
I want Joe Frazier.

588
00:23:37,700 --> 00:23:40,300
(upbeat music)

589
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:45,767
(chuckling)

590
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:47,300
- Oh, that's fun.
- It makes you feel good.

591
00:23:47,333 --> 00:23:48,400
- [Crow] I'm sorry.

592
00:23:48,433 --> 00:23:49,633
Hey, it's a
personal-pan Hercules.

593
00:23:49,667 --> 00:23:51,000
- [Tom] Herc on a
raft, wreck 'em.

594
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:54,133
- Hercules!

595
00:23:58,667 --> 00:24:02,167
♪ Little Audrey's day ♪

596
00:24:02,200 --> 00:24:03,400
What?

597
00:24:03,433 --> 00:24:04,867
I'm trying to get a
little shut eye here.

598
00:24:04,900 --> 00:24:06,167
- Hercules!
- I'm the Herc.

599
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,333
- [Tom] Oh, Vic Damone.

600
00:24:08,267 --> 00:24:09,967
- Hercules!
(yelling)

601
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,100
- [Crow] Oh.

602
00:24:11,133 --> 00:24:14,033
(yelling)

603
00:24:14,067 --> 00:24:15,667
- [Hercules] Oh omnipotent Zeus.

604
00:24:17,033 --> 00:24:18,767
- [Tom] Hi, Zeus is
not in right now,

605
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:21,567
but if you'd like to
leave a message...

606
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:22,800
- Hear my plea.

607
00:24:22,833 --> 00:24:24,500
- [Crow] Not guilty
by reason of insanity.

608
00:24:24,533 --> 00:24:26,500
- If Androcles is still alive.

609
00:24:26,533 --> 00:24:29,433
♪ In the year 3535 ♪

610
00:24:30,867 --> 00:24:32,667
- Grant me that we
might meet again.

611
00:24:33,867 --> 00:24:37,633
- [Tom] You think we
could pan with him here?

612
00:24:38,667 --> 00:24:40,200
- Oh Zeus, my father.

613
00:24:40,233 --> 00:24:44,500
- [Crow] I'm not your real
father, it was Poseidon.

614
00:24:48,300 --> 00:24:50,100
(coughing)

615
00:24:50,133 --> 00:24:53,767
- [Joel] Herc, don't swim until
an hour after you've slept.

616
00:24:58,167 --> 00:25:01,100
- [Crow] Even in the water
Murray's wigs don't come off.

617
00:25:02,600 --> 00:25:05,400
- [Joel] Oh, I recognize
that, that's from Star Trek.

618
00:25:05,433 --> 00:25:06,867
- [Crow] Oh yeah.

619
00:25:08,300 --> 00:25:10,900
- [Joel] He's landed on
the Captain Crunch Island.

620
00:25:10,933 --> 00:25:12,133
- [Tom] Rock Candy baby.

621
00:25:13,333 --> 00:25:17,067
This isn't gonna be so bad.
(chuckling)

622
00:25:17,100 --> 00:25:19,367
- [Crow] Say, are
you a captive woman?

623
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:21,767
- Kill me.
- With kindness.

624
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:23,333
- Kill me, I beg you.

625
00:25:23,367 --> 00:25:25,567
- Do not fear, I
will not harm you.

626
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:28,133
- Please put an end
to this torment.

627
00:25:28,167 --> 00:25:29,000
Kill me.

628
00:25:30,467 --> 00:25:31,667
- I love you like a rock.
- What god persecutes you?

629
00:25:31,700 --> 00:25:34,367
- Go away, stranger, go away.

630
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:35,867
- Who has imprisoned you?

631
00:25:35,900 --> 00:25:38,333
- He was a man like you
but he can be everything,

632
00:25:38,367 --> 00:25:42,033
a great serpent, water,
a terrible tempest.

633
00:25:42,067 --> 00:25:43,233
- All men are alike.
- The air that you breathe,

634
00:25:43,267 --> 00:25:45,633
the earth you walk
upon, go away.

635
00:25:45,667 --> 00:25:47,933
No one knows in what
form he will next appear.

636
00:25:47,967 --> 00:25:50,000
- Who is the monster
who threatens you?

637
00:25:50,033 --> 00:25:51,833
- Proteus.
- Protein?

638
00:25:51,867 --> 00:25:53,733
He's pure protein?
- Watch out!

639
00:25:53,767 --> 00:25:54,967
- Is that him?
- Save yourself!

640
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:58,167
It's him, it's Proteus!
- Behind the old man?

641
00:26:00,067 --> 00:26:02,267
- Go away.
- Leon Russell?

642
00:26:02,300 --> 00:26:05,633
- I don't want
intruders on my island.

643
00:26:05,667 --> 00:26:06,933
- [Crow] But sir, if
you'd just consider

644
00:26:06,967 --> 00:26:08,467
these magazine subscriptions.

645
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:10,467
- Or you'll be
dead by nightfall.

646
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:13,033
(ominous music)
(thunder booming)

647
00:26:13,067 --> 00:26:14,133
- Oh no!
- Ah!

648
00:26:15,567 --> 00:26:17,900
- [Tom] Oh, they're
on the Far Side.

649
00:26:17,933 --> 00:26:19,133
- [Crow] They got a dog.

650
00:26:24,033 --> 00:26:25,667
- [Joel] Watch out
for the backdraft

651
00:26:25,700 --> 00:26:27,867
'cause it isn't that good.

652
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:30,067
(yelling)

653
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:34,800
- [Crow] Now Herc's doing his
Nastassja Kinski impression.

654
00:26:34,833 --> 00:26:35,933
Snakes away.

655
00:26:35,967 --> 00:26:38,633
- [Joel] Sit Booboo, sit, stay.

656
00:26:38,667 --> 00:26:39,833
(roaring)

657
00:26:39,867 --> 00:26:41,567
- Kitty.
- Suddenly it's an MGM film.

658
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,767
(roaring)

659
00:26:45,033 --> 00:26:48,433
- [Crow] What'd you
have to hit me for?

660
00:26:48,467 --> 00:26:50,200
- [Tom] Hey, it's
Lion Buscaglia.

661
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:51,567
(laughing)
- Hey.

662
00:26:51,600 --> 00:26:52,700
- [Tom] Give me a hug.

663
00:26:53,933 --> 00:26:55,967
- Basic Instinct.
- I'll say.

664
00:26:59,267 --> 00:27:01,367
- Hey!
(laughing)

665
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:03,300
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

666
00:27:03,333 --> 00:27:04,533
(gobbling)

667
00:27:04,567 --> 00:27:06,600
It's the turkey
from Room Service!

668
00:27:06,633 --> 00:27:08,867
- [Crow] Now he's Tippi Hendren.

669
00:27:08,900 --> 00:27:12,200
- [Joel] Watch out for the
string, Herc, it'll cut ya!

670
00:27:14,333 --> 00:27:16,600
(gobbling)

671
00:27:17,733 --> 00:27:18,933
- [Crow] Hah, I'm back!

672
00:27:18,967 --> 00:27:20,800
I'll be your tour
guide through Hell!

673
00:27:21,867 --> 00:27:24,267
(chattering)

674
00:27:24,300 --> 00:27:25,400
- [Joel] Dino.

675
00:27:25,433 --> 00:27:27,967
Steam dragon,
steamin' mad at Herc.

676
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,167
(chuckling)

677
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:30,667
- [Crow] Daryl Dragon.

678
00:27:30,700 --> 00:27:33,300
- [Joel] I love it when men
and lizards fight over me.

679
00:27:34,367 --> 00:27:36,067
- [Tom] Herc's gonna get warts.

680
00:27:36,100 --> 00:27:38,700
(chuckling)

681
00:27:38,733 --> 00:27:41,633
Young and beautiful, some
day your looks will be gone.

682
00:27:41,667 --> 00:27:45,567
(chuckling)
It's Gordon Gecko.

683
00:27:47,633 --> 00:27:49,933
- [Crow] I'm not slimy,
take it back, take it back!

684
00:27:49,967 --> 00:27:52,900
- [Joel] Oh, he's a karma
chameleon, they come and go.

685
00:27:52,933 --> 00:27:54,133
- They come and go.
- Mm-hmm.

686
00:27:54,167 --> 00:27:55,967
- [Tom] Look, I'm just
not a touchy person.

687
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:58,367
(groaning)

688
00:27:58,400 --> 00:28:00,500
- [Crow] Note to
myself, next time,

689
00:28:00,533 --> 00:28:02,267
turn into something
without a horn.

690
00:28:03,433 --> 00:28:05,500
- [Tom] Ooh, you are
one spooky lizard.

691
00:28:07,667 --> 00:28:11,000
- [Joel] Oh, he's gonna need
some Neosporin, definitely.

692
00:28:11,033 --> 00:28:12,467
Ugh.

693
00:28:12,500 --> 00:28:14,367
- [Crow] I'm sorry I did
that, that's so disgusting.

694
00:28:16,633 --> 00:28:17,700
- [Joel] Hmm.

695
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,067
- Say.
- Well now you're free.

696
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:22,167
Oops.

697
00:28:23,167 --> 00:28:24,333
- [Tom] Hello?

698
00:28:25,967 --> 00:28:28,867
I guess you can get
blood from a stone, huh?

699
00:28:30,267 --> 00:28:31,467
- [Crow] Boy, the graffiti's
gettin' bad around here.

700
00:28:31,500 --> 00:28:32,333
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

701
00:28:34,867 --> 00:28:36,633
- [Tom] U2, live at Red Rocks.

702
00:28:37,900 --> 00:28:39,867
- I'm saved.
- Yes, Proteus is dead.

703
00:28:40,900 --> 00:28:41,800
That is his blood.

704
00:28:43,233 --> 00:28:45,667
This rocky cliff, the whole
island is Proteus himself.

705
00:28:45,700 --> 00:28:46,900
- [Joel] Wow, he's big!

706
00:28:46,933 --> 00:28:48,167
- He nourished himself
on the blood of you

707
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:50,667
and other victims,
but now it's all over.

708
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:54,367
- You think so?

709
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:56,200
It was my people who
left me as a sacrifice

710
00:28:56,233 --> 00:28:57,467
to prevent him from
destroying them.

711
00:28:57,500 --> 00:28:59,000
- [Tom] Oh, nice.

712
00:28:59,033 --> 00:29:01,800
- When you killed him you went
against the will of the gods.

713
00:29:01,833 --> 00:29:03,333
- [Tom] It was cool!

714
00:29:03,367 --> 00:29:05,467
- Without the help of the gods
I would never have succeeded

715
00:29:05,500 --> 00:29:07,900
in slaying that monster.
- Buy me a drink?

716
00:29:07,933 --> 00:29:10,033
- And the gods
will help us again.

717
00:29:10,067 --> 00:29:12,400
- [Joel] Like this
beautiful breeze they sent.

718
00:29:12,433 --> 00:29:14,133
(ethereal music)

719
00:29:14,167 --> 00:29:16,900
♪ The Simpsons ♪

720
00:29:16,933 --> 00:29:19,367
(vocalizing)

721
00:29:19,400 --> 00:29:22,000
- There's my country, Atlantis!

722
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:24,367
- [Joel] Atlantis?

723
00:29:24,400 --> 00:29:26,600
Oh, that's where the
Superstation comes from.

724
00:29:26,633 --> 00:29:28,300
- [Tom] Conveniently
located too.

725
00:29:29,500 --> 00:29:33,067
Looks like a race of polyps.
(groaning)

726
00:29:36,500 --> 00:29:38,600
- [Crow] Well, I'm glad
they hired sim security.

727
00:29:42,700 --> 00:29:44,000
- [Tom] Hey.

728
00:29:44,033 --> 00:29:46,433
(vocalizing)

729
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:53,700
- [Crow] It's like everyone's
lost their contacts.

730
00:29:53,733 --> 00:29:56,700
(chuckling)
They're looking for them.

731
00:29:56,733 --> 00:29:59,233
(vocalizing)

732
00:30:02,900 --> 00:30:04,400
- [Joel] Wait for
me, wait for me!

733
00:30:04,433 --> 00:30:07,233
I know I have one credit left
but I'm missing my graduation!

734
00:30:09,933 --> 00:30:11,867
- Today is dedicated to Uranus.

735
00:30:11,900 --> 00:30:13,400
- Well thank you, I'm flat--
- The queen is in the temple

736
00:30:13,433 --> 00:30:15,100
for the sacred ceremony.

737
00:30:16,567 --> 00:30:19,000
- [Joel] Can I keep my thong on?

738
00:30:19,033 --> 00:30:21,133
- [Tom] Geez, for me
I better beat cheeks.

739
00:30:24,433 --> 00:30:26,067
- [Crow] Everyone get down
and praise Hercules' anus!

740
00:30:26,100 --> 00:30:28,333
- [Joel] That's not
what they meant.

741
00:30:28,367 --> 00:30:30,667
- Well that's what she said.
- I know, but...

742
00:30:31,767 --> 00:30:33,933
- [Tom] Hey, Jim
Henson's Gandhi Babies.

743
00:30:34,900 --> 00:30:36,933
- No, no, my only son, no!

744
00:30:38,167 --> 00:30:40,500
They can't take my son from me!

745
00:30:40,533 --> 00:30:42,233
- I hate hecklers.
- No, no, no!

746
00:30:43,533 --> 00:30:44,867
- [Tom] Conform,
come on, conform.

747
00:30:44,900 --> 00:30:47,500
- And those children
are dedicated to Uranus.

748
00:30:47,533 --> 00:30:49,967
They're going to the
Mountain of the Dead.

749
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:51,600
- [Crow] Wow, that's
cool, is that a Six Flags'

750
00:30:51,633 --> 00:30:52,967
Mountain of the Dead?

751
00:30:54,200 --> 00:30:55,633
(triumphant music)

752
00:30:55,667 --> 00:30:56,867
- [Tom] Ladies and
gentlemen, please welcome

753
00:30:56,900 --> 00:31:01,867
the King family.
(applauding)

754
00:31:02,800 --> 00:31:05,233
(vocalizing)

755
00:31:07,167 --> 00:31:08,167
- [Crow] Look at
that guy up there.

756
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:09,433
(groaning)

757
00:31:09,467 --> 00:31:12,200
Hey, could somebody
help me with this thing?

758
00:31:12,233 --> 00:31:14,733
- [Joel] Excellent
copper buffalo shot.

759
00:31:15,867 --> 00:31:16,900
- [Tom] Hey look, they
worship the cuckoo

760
00:31:16,933 --> 00:31:18,700
for Cocoa Puffs guy.

761
00:31:18,733 --> 00:31:21,400
(ominous music)

762
00:31:22,967 --> 00:31:26,667
- [Joel] You kids take those
horses outside right now!

763
00:31:26,700 --> 00:31:28,667
- [Crow] All right, fill
'em up and give me a lube

764
00:31:28,700 --> 00:31:30,700
and a wash and wash
the inside too.

765
00:31:30,733 --> 00:31:33,400
♪ Here comes the king, here
comes the big number one ♪

766
00:31:33,433 --> 00:31:34,867
(vocalizing)

767
00:31:34,900 --> 00:31:36,800
- Antinea.
- Hi, I'm a new character.

768
00:31:36,833 --> 00:31:38,900
- Forgive me if I
interrupt the ceremony,

769
00:31:38,933 --> 00:31:41,133
but the mists that protect
our island have vanished

770
00:31:41,167 --> 00:31:42,667
as if by magic.
- Say, who's the new girl?

771
00:31:42,700 --> 00:31:45,000
- I saw it from the mountain.

772
00:31:45,033 --> 00:31:47,933
It's now my fear that Atlantis
can be seen by mortal eyes.

773
00:31:49,367 --> 00:31:51,233
- Uranus has abandoned us!
- Speak for yourself!

774
00:31:51,267 --> 00:31:52,733
- That explains his anger.

775
00:31:52,767 --> 00:31:55,267
Listen to the thunder over
on the great mountain!

776
00:31:56,233 --> 00:31:58,500
We must sacrifice to Proteus.

777
00:31:58,533 --> 00:31:59,300
- Wait!

778
00:32:00,767 --> 00:32:02,833
Proteus does not need
human victims any longer.

779
00:32:02,867 --> 00:32:05,167
- You dare interfere,
who are you?

780
00:32:05,200 --> 00:32:07,000
- Hercules of Thebes!
- My card!

781
00:32:07,033 --> 00:32:09,033
- My father, the omnipotent
Zeus, has guided me here

782
00:32:09,067 --> 00:32:11,100
to your land!
(suspenseful music)

783
00:32:11,133 --> 00:32:12,767
- [Tom] Hey, you guys are
supposed to be nice to me,

784
00:32:12,800 --> 00:32:15,300
today is dedicated to my--
- We know.

785
00:32:15,333 --> 00:32:16,167
(groaning)

786
00:32:16,200 --> 00:32:17,600
- [Crow] Gymkata!

787
00:32:18,800 --> 00:32:19,733
- Let him alone.

788
00:32:21,733 --> 00:32:23,567
No mortal has ever
dared set foot

789
00:32:23,600 --> 00:32:25,967
on the sacred island
of Atlantis before.

790
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:28,267
- [Joel] Well, she's got
a point, guys, let's blow.

791
00:32:28,300 --> 00:32:30,267
- What are you doing here?
- Selling band candy.

792
00:32:30,300 --> 00:32:32,400
- What foolhardy reason
has led you to defy

793
00:32:32,433 --> 00:32:33,700
the ire of our god?

794
00:32:34,567 --> 00:32:36,200
- I do not believe in evil gods,

795
00:32:36,233 --> 00:32:38,200
such gods I have
been taught to hate.

796
00:32:38,233 --> 00:32:40,533
I forbid gods which
demand human sacrifices--

797
00:32:40,567 --> 00:32:42,033
- Cool painting.
- And slake their thirst

798
00:32:42,067 --> 00:32:45,067
with human blood, for this
reason I have slain Proteus

799
00:32:45,100 --> 00:32:46,867
and saved the life of a maiden--

800
00:32:46,900 --> 00:32:47,933
- Joanne Woodward.
- Who was sacrificed

801
00:32:47,967 --> 00:32:50,667
to his monstrous fury.
- You lie!

802
00:32:50,700 --> 00:32:51,933
- [Crow] Oh!

803
00:32:51,967 --> 00:32:53,467
- [Tom] Maybe I
do, maybe I don't

804
00:32:53,500 --> 00:32:56,100
all I know is I'm
outta here, bye.

805
00:32:56,133 --> 00:32:57,467
- [Joel] Kristy McNichol?

806
00:32:57,500 --> 00:33:00,267
(gasping)
- Wow.

807
00:33:00,300 --> 00:33:01,767
- I'm here, mother.

808
00:33:01,800 --> 00:33:04,367
(upbeat music)

809
00:33:07,567 --> 00:33:11,033
- There was no need to sacrifice
the daughter of a queen.

810
00:33:11,067 --> 00:33:13,433
(gentle instrumental music)

811
00:33:13,467 --> 00:33:16,400
You are the daughter of Antinea.

812
00:33:16,433 --> 00:33:18,100
You are my daughter.

813
00:33:19,267 --> 00:33:21,700
If you had to die--
- I wouldn't mind.

814
00:33:21,733 --> 00:33:24,800
- It was for a far more noble
and fatal reason than that.

815
00:33:24,833 --> 00:33:27,833
- [Tom] 'Tis a far, far better
thing than I have ever done.

816
00:33:28,767 --> 00:33:30,533
- What reason?

817
00:33:30,567 --> 00:33:33,367
- Your destiny is
bound to mine, Ismene.

818
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:35,733
Just as mine is
bound to my kingdom.

819
00:33:35,767 --> 00:33:37,633
- [Joel] And my kingdom
is bound to Fred's kingdom

820
00:33:37,667 --> 00:33:40,167
and Fred's kingdom is
bound to Murray's kingdom.

821
00:33:40,200 --> 00:33:42,067
- Have the same meaning for me,

822
00:33:42,100 --> 00:33:44,833
unfortunately
nothing has changed.

823
00:33:44,867 --> 00:33:46,433
On the day that a
daughter of mine

824
00:33:46,467 --> 00:33:49,133
shall survive me, it is
written in the sacred books

825
00:33:49,167 --> 00:33:50,567
Atlantis shall be destroyed.

826
00:33:51,433 --> 00:33:53,000
- Mother, then I...

827
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:55,467
- You must die.

828
00:33:55,500 --> 00:33:57,167
- [Crow] Boy, she's
really strict.

829
00:33:59,267 --> 00:34:03,000
- No, I don't want to die.
- I want to live!

830
00:34:03,033 --> 00:34:06,700
I want to live and laugh and
love at life and and live!

831
00:34:06,733 --> 00:34:08,700
(crying)

832
00:34:08,733 --> 00:34:10,867
- [Joel] You stop or I'll give
you something to cry about.

833
00:34:10,900 --> 00:34:13,200
(crying)
- Take her away.

834
00:34:14,367 --> 00:34:15,533
- [Tom] And if you
don't die willingly,

835
00:34:15,567 --> 00:34:17,267
I'm going to ground
you, young lady.

836
00:34:22,200 --> 00:34:23,700
- I really admire what
you did back there,

837
00:34:23,733 --> 00:34:25,500
just wanted to say
that, not because,

838
00:34:25,533 --> 00:34:27,400
there's gonna be three
extra people for dinner,

839
00:34:27,433 --> 00:34:29,767
should I, oh never mind,
I'll come back later.

840
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:31,533
We're outta here, let's go.

841
00:34:31,567 --> 00:34:35,000
(suspenseful music)

842
00:34:35,033 --> 00:34:37,467
(vocalizing)

843
00:34:43,767 --> 00:34:46,467
- John?
- Marsha

844
00:34:46,500 --> 00:34:48,500
- John!
- Marsha!

845
00:34:48,533 --> 00:34:50,200
- Oh John!
- Marsha!

846
00:34:50,233 --> 00:34:51,400
- John, John, John!
- Marsha, Marsha, Marsha!

847
00:34:55,633 --> 00:34:56,833
- [Tom] John, Marsha.

848
00:34:56,867 --> 00:34:58,333
(distorted warbling)

849
00:34:58,367 --> 00:34:59,933
- [Joel] Oh, he bumped into
the invisible synthesizer.

850
00:34:59,967 --> 00:35:00,967
- [Tom] Ooh!

851
00:35:04,567 --> 00:35:06,567
- [Crow] Ah, you
wouldn't understand.

852
00:35:08,233 --> 00:35:09,133
- Androcles, wait!

853
00:35:12,200 --> 00:35:15,000
Androcles, why didn't you--
- Oh, hay fever huh?

854
00:35:15,033 --> 00:35:16,633
(whistling)

855
00:35:16,667 --> 00:35:17,800
- [Joel] Gosh, I'm sorry,

856
00:35:17,833 --> 00:35:20,400
I thought you were
someone I used to date.

857
00:35:20,433 --> 00:35:22,200
(mysterious music)

858
00:35:22,233 --> 00:35:24,600
- No, it's not possible.
- What is not possible?

859
00:35:24,633 --> 00:35:26,933
- [Crow] Going faster
than the speed of light?

860
00:35:27,800 --> 00:35:28,633
- That man.

861
00:35:30,533 --> 00:35:33,867
I saw myself it was Androcles.
- Androcles?

862
00:35:33,900 --> 00:35:35,300
I don't understand.
(scoffing)

863
00:35:35,333 --> 00:35:38,233
- Androcles, A N D R--
- I don't understand myself.

864
00:35:38,267 --> 00:35:40,233
I'm sure I saw my
friend Androcles.

865
00:35:41,367 --> 00:35:42,867
And yet...

866
00:35:42,900 --> 00:35:46,067
- I don't doubt your words.
- Just your intelligence.

867
00:35:46,100 --> 00:35:47,867
- I suppose you think
I've lost my mind?

868
00:35:47,900 --> 00:35:50,267
Even I now seem only
to have dreamed it all.

869
00:35:50,300 --> 00:35:52,000
- [Crow] A planet where
apes evolved from--

870
00:35:52,033 --> 00:35:55,067
- Quite normal, often the
desire to see a loved one

871
00:35:55,100 --> 00:35:57,600
creates the illusion
of seeing visions.

872
00:35:57,633 --> 00:35:59,700
- Thank you Dr Joyce Brothers.
- Yes, perhaps you're right.

873
00:35:59,733 --> 00:36:02,767
- Besides, you are weary
from your long journey,

874
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:05,767
seeing nothing but death
and hardship along the way.

875
00:36:05,800 --> 00:36:07,867
You might relax and
put your mind at peace

876
00:36:07,900 --> 00:36:09,167
with more pleasant things.

877
00:36:09,200 --> 00:36:10,267
- [Joel] Why does
she always have

878
00:36:10,300 --> 00:36:12,733
a Catholic processional
behind her?

879
00:36:12,767 --> 00:36:14,367
- [Tom] Don't know.

880
00:36:17,033 --> 00:36:19,967
♪ Standing on a beach
with a gun in my hand ♪

881
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:21,533
- [Crow] Wake up,
Linda Hunt is here!

882
00:36:21,567 --> 00:36:23,867
- Hylas, wake up, there
are horsemen coming!

883
00:36:23,900 --> 00:36:25,500
- Would you leave me in peace?

884
00:36:25,533 --> 00:36:27,500
I've been waiting for this
for days, now I wanna sleep.

885
00:36:27,533 --> 00:36:28,900
- [Tom] Christopher Walken.

886
00:36:30,267 --> 00:36:31,767
- Get up, they're coming closer!

887
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:33,400
One of the men is carrying
a girl with him, it looks

888
00:36:33,433 --> 00:36:35,233
like she's a prisoner.
- A girl?

889
00:36:35,267 --> 00:36:37,733
- [Crow] A girl, I'm
a Grimwald warrior!

890
00:36:39,100 --> 00:36:40,833
- [Joel] How's my 'do?

891
00:36:40,867 --> 00:36:41,767
- [Crow] It'll do.

892
00:36:42,967 --> 00:36:44,567
- [Tom] I tell ya, this
would really be exciting

893
00:36:44,600 --> 00:36:46,100
if I knew what was going on.

894
00:36:47,433 --> 00:36:48,733
Smoke bomb.

895
00:36:48,767 --> 00:36:52,467
(suspenseful music)

896
00:36:52,500 --> 00:36:54,100
- [Joel] Oh look, somebody
threw a cherry bomb

897
00:36:54,133 --> 00:36:56,067
over there.
- Oh, cool.

898
00:36:56,100 --> 00:36:57,267
- [Tom] Right in the toilet.

899
00:36:57,300 --> 00:36:58,733
- Put her down and
tie her to that stake.

900
00:36:58,767 --> 00:37:00,867
- [Crow] I'm tired of
steak too, I want chicken!

901
00:37:00,900 --> 00:37:01,700
Oh.

902
00:37:05,800 --> 00:37:08,200
- [Tom] Sir, did you get
your validation sticker?

903
00:37:12,867 --> 00:37:15,167
- Why wait 'til sunset,
let's kill her now.

904
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:17,900
- And beat the rush.
- That's orders of Antinea.

905
00:37:17,933 --> 00:37:20,433
(suspenseful music)

906
00:37:20,467 --> 00:37:22,100
When it's time, we'll
throw her from the cliffs

907
00:37:22,133 --> 00:37:23,667
to the rocks below.

908
00:37:23,700 --> 00:37:25,433
Don't you look at me like that.

909
00:37:25,467 --> 00:37:26,833
We're merely
obeying your mother.

910
00:37:26,867 --> 00:37:28,267
- [Crow] I was only
following orders,

911
00:37:28,300 --> 00:37:30,333
I love my adopted country!

912
00:37:30,367 --> 00:37:31,933
- What are you doing?
- I'm saving that girl,

913
00:37:31,967 --> 00:37:33,433
do you want to see 'em kill her?

914
00:37:33,467 --> 00:37:35,267
- No, but I don't wanna save
her by getting killed myself.

915
00:37:35,300 --> 00:37:38,300
- I have my rights, I have my
rights, his name was Callahan!

916
00:37:39,800 --> 00:37:41,700
- [Joel] Pizza pizza.

917
00:37:41,733 --> 00:37:43,267
(groaning)

918
00:37:43,300 --> 00:37:46,567
(suspenseful music)

919
00:37:46,600 --> 00:37:49,500
I've got a headache
this big and it's oof.

920
00:37:50,900 --> 00:37:52,200
- [Crow] Head Injury
Playhouse says,

921
00:37:52,233 --> 00:37:53,767
"Don't let this happen to you."

922
00:37:55,067 --> 00:37:56,367
- [Tom] He's dead, Jim.

923
00:37:57,233 --> 00:38:00,300
(suspenseful music)

924
00:38:03,500 --> 00:38:04,533
Hey.

925
00:38:04,567 --> 00:38:06,100
♪ They smile in your face ♪

926
00:38:06,133 --> 00:38:08,333
♪ All the time they want
to take your place ♪

927
00:38:08,367 --> 00:38:10,333
♪ Backstabbers ♪

928
00:38:10,367 --> 00:38:12,533
(yelling)

929
00:38:14,500 --> 00:38:18,500
- [Tom] Exit, stage left,
Heavens to Murgatroyd.

930
00:38:18,533 --> 00:38:21,533
(suspenseful music)

931
00:38:24,200 --> 00:38:26,300
- [Crow] I see
London, I see France.

932
00:38:26,333 --> 00:38:28,367
- [Tom] Lot more than that.

933
00:38:28,400 --> 00:38:31,667
♪ Everybody must get stoned ♪

934
00:38:31,700 --> 00:38:34,700
- [Tom] Tonight's episode,
Jack and Jill when up the hill

935
00:38:34,733 --> 00:38:36,733
to fetch a pail of murder.

936
00:38:36,767 --> 00:38:39,767
(suspenseful music)

937
00:38:43,333 --> 00:38:45,333
- Are there any others?
- No, I speared the last one.

938
00:38:45,367 --> 00:38:47,700
- [Crow] I have my
rights, I have my rights!

939
00:38:47,733 --> 00:38:49,467
- [Joel] That's good.

940
00:38:50,767 --> 00:38:53,433
- [Crow] Ooh, dibs, I call dibs!

941
00:38:54,867 --> 00:38:56,533
- [Tom] It takes me longer
'cause my legs are shorter.

942
00:38:56,567 --> 00:38:58,633
- We're here to protect you.
- Courage!

943
00:38:58,667 --> 00:39:00,633
- It's no use, it's no use.
- Why say that?

944
00:39:00,667 --> 00:39:02,033
- [Crow] I can't make a decent

945
00:39:02,067 --> 00:39:03,400
cup of coffee.
- Where can I go?

946
00:39:05,467 --> 00:39:08,000
No matter where, it's my
destiny that I die now.

947
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:12,033
- Don't be foolish,
who'd wanna kill you?

948
00:39:12,067 --> 00:39:13,667
What kind of people live here?

949
00:39:13,700 --> 00:39:15,667
- Unfriendly and
somewhat nervous.

950
00:39:15,700 --> 00:39:18,400
- Fly for your lives at
once, they'll kill you too.

951
00:39:19,833 --> 00:39:22,433
They've possibly already
killed the great Hercules.

952
00:39:22,467 --> 00:39:25,300
- Hercules, is he far away?

953
00:39:25,333 --> 00:39:27,267
- Do you know him?
- Know him?

954
00:39:27,300 --> 00:39:30,000
He was in my physics class!
- Don't worry now.

955
00:39:30,033 --> 00:39:33,000
If he's here we're all safe.
- I'm a little drummer boy.

956
00:39:34,200 --> 00:39:35,433
Oh wow.
- Fondue?

957
00:39:40,500 --> 00:39:42,233
- [Tom] Ladies and gentlemen,
we are proud to introduce

958
00:39:42,267 --> 00:39:44,267
the June Taylor Dancers.

959
00:39:45,600 --> 00:39:47,967
(vocalizing)

960
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:50,567
- [Crow] Hah, they're dancing
to Uncle Meat by Frank Zappa.

961
00:39:50,600 --> 00:39:53,133
- [Tom] Sounds like Dog Breath,
in the Year of the Plague.

962
00:39:53,167 --> 00:39:57,100
♪ Primer me carucha, Chevy '39 ♪

963
00:39:58,633 --> 00:40:00,000
- [Joel] Oh, Richard Pryor.

964
00:40:02,967 --> 00:40:05,300
They die for their art.

965
00:40:05,333 --> 00:40:06,533
- We in Greece--
- D Y E.

966
00:40:06,567 --> 00:40:08,067
- Are interested in
the graces in art,

967
00:40:08,100 --> 00:40:09,333
those magical apparitions.

968
00:40:09,367 --> 00:40:10,533
- [Tom] Please sir,
keep the table talk

969
00:40:10,567 --> 00:40:11,467
to a minimum.
- What you witness

970
