(groaning)
- Oh, why?

1435
01:00:33,533 --> 01:00:35,467
- The rock of the gods
will only lose its power

1436
01:00:35,500 --> 01:00:38,867
when touched by a force
above and beyond this Earth

1437
01:00:38,900 --> 01:00:40,367
on which we live.

1438
01:00:40,400 --> 01:00:42,433
- You know the secret of
this force, Zayned, tell me.

1439
01:00:42,467 --> 01:00:44,433
- [Crow] It's pudding,
I don't know why.

1440
01:00:47,100 --> 01:00:49,867
- I can reveal to only one
man the secret mysteries

1441
01:00:49,900 --> 01:00:51,133
of the gods but he must show me

1442
01:00:51,167 --> 01:00:53,900
that he is stronger
than the rock itself.

1443
01:00:53,933 --> 01:00:55,800
Take this bar, Hercules.

1444
01:00:55,833 --> 01:00:57,733
- [Tom] Keep it as
my free gift to you.

1445
01:01:04,067 --> 01:01:05,633
- [Crow] That's it,
that's all he has to do?

1446
01:01:05,667 --> 01:01:07,000
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

1447
01:01:09,467 --> 01:01:12,433
This Hercules is
dumber than I remember.

1448
01:01:12,467 --> 01:01:15,100
(intense music)

1449
01:01:15,133 --> 01:01:17,467
- [Crow] So you took
shop class, big deal.

1450
01:01:18,600 --> 01:01:19,733
- [Tom] He's dreamy.

1451
01:01:24,000 --> 01:01:27,367
- Zeus, Father, help me.

1452
01:01:27,400 --> 01:01:28,300
- [Crow] Help me, Zeus.

1453
01:01:28,333 --> 01:01:30,667
- I do not do this out of pride.

1454
01:01:30,700 --> 01:01:31,667
This you know.

1455
01:01:32,833 --> 01:01:34,867
It is only to cause
their hearts of stone

1456
01:01:34,900 --> 01:01:36,767
to swell up with pity.

1457
01:01:36,800 --> 01:01:39,000
To let their eyes
fill with tears,

1458
01:01:39,033 --> 01:01:40,667
the tears of common humanity.

1459
01:01:41,867 --> 01:01:43,867
Do not abandon me in this trial.

1460
01:01:43,900 --> 01:01:45,333
- [Tom] Oh nice, you
know, this would make

1461
01:01:45,367 --> 01:01:48,200
another good monologue for
young American actors on the go.

1462
01:01:48,233 --> 01:01:51,100
(mysterious music)

1463
01:01:53,733 --> 01:01:55,967
- [Joel] Hercules is
seeking the perfect tan.

1464
01:01:56,900 --> 01:01:58,267
- Edna too.
- You've won,

1465
01:01:58,300 --> 01:02:00,233
Hercules of Thebes.

1466
01:02:00,267 --> 01:02:02,867
Only the rays of the sun can
destroy the rock of Uranus.

1467
01:02:02,900 --> 01:02:04,300
- You need more fiber.
- When a man can remove

1468
01:02:04,333 --> 01:02:07,700
that stone and a ray of
sunlight shines upon the rock,

1469
01:02:07,733 --> 01:02:10,833
then we will see the reign
of Antinea of Atlantis.

1470
01:02:10,867 --> 01:02:13,000
(gasping)
And of all its inhabitants.

1471
01:02:13,033 --> 01:02:15,467
- Thank you, Zayned,
and have no fear.

1472
01:02:15,500 --> 01:02:17,900
I shall succeed in
defeating Antinea,

1473
01:02:17,933 --> 01:02:20,767
without destroying Atlantis
or her inhabitants.

1474
01:02:20,800 --> 01:02:22,000
- [Tom] Okay.

1475
01:02:22,033 --> 01:02:22,933
- With the help
of my companions,

1476
01:02:22,967 --> 01:02:24,200
I shall put an end to her reign.

1477
01:02:24,233 --> 01:02:25,433
(yelling)

1478
01:02:25,467 --> 01:02:27,533
- [Crow] That's us,
we're his companions!

1479
01:02:27,567 --> 01:02:30,567
- [Tom] Companions
of Hercules, woo!

1480
01:02:31,500 --> 01:02:32,567
- [Joel] Huh?

1481
01:02:35,433 --> 01:02:38,200
A funny thing happened
on the way to the forum.

1482
01:02:38,233 --> 01:02:40,733
- [Tom] They made
a Hercules movie!

1483
01:02:40,767 --> 01:02:42,767
(vocalizing)
- Remember the Alamo!

1484
01:02:42,800 --> 01:02:46,500
- Storm the Bastille!
- Give us Barabbas!

1485
01:02:46,533 --> 01:02:50,433
- Hell no, we won't go!
- Attica, Attica!

1486
01:02:50,467 --> 01:02:51,700
- [Crow] Oh.

1487
01:02:51,733 --> 01:02:54,333
- [Tom] Atticus, so you
want a revolution huh?

1488
01:02:54,367 --> 01:02:56,100
- [Joel] That's what it's
like tryin' to get into

1489
01:02:56,133 --> 01:02:57,700
Let's Make a Deal.
- Ooh.

1490
01:03:02,467 --> 01:03:03,867
Well I see our neighbors
are at it again.

1491
01:03:03,900 --> 01:03:04,733
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

1492
01:03:06,967 --> 01:03:07,767
Should I call the cops?

1493
01:03:07,800 --> 01:03:09,433
I'll call the cops.

1494
01:03:09,467 --> 01:03:12,467
(suspenseful music)

1495
01:03:16,133 --> 01:03:19,167
- [Tom] Looks like a job for
the Arthur Rank Organisation.

1496
01:03:20,567 --> 01:03:21,567
- [Crow] No more
than three items

1497
01:03:21,600 --> 01:03:23,067
in the fitting rooms, please.

1498
01:03:25,633 --> 01:03:26,833
- [Tom] Is that our cue?

1499
01:03:26,867 --> 01:03:28,233
That's our cue, come on
boys, that's our cue.

1500
01:03:29,733 --> 01:03:32,067
- [Joel] Okay, everybody,
let's have fun this time.

1501
01:03:32,100 --> 01:03:33,533
Come on!

1502
01:03:33,567 --> 01:03:38,567
♪ One singular sensation,
every little one ♪

1503
01:03:39,967 --> 01:03:42,167
- [Crow] Had this been an
actual emergency, you would...

1504
01:03:42,200 --> 01:03:45,533
♪ We love you Conrad ♪

1505
01:03:45,567 --> 01:03:47,967
♪ Oh yes we do ♪

1506
01:03:48,000 --> 01:03:49,733
- [Crow] Parthenon party!

1507
01:03:49,767 --> 01:03:50,700
- [Tom] I guess so.

1508
01:03:51,867 --> 01:03:53,200
- [Joel] Well they
stopped the revolution

1509
01:03:53,233 --> 01:03:55,233
to take a little nap, I see.

1510
01:03:55,267 --> 01:03:57,433
(snoring)

1511
01:04:00,300 --> 01:04:01,567
- Very good, Joel.
- Thank you.

1512
01:04:01,600 --> 01:04:05,367
- The money's in the...
(groaning)

1513
01:04:05,400 --> 01:04:07,833
- [Joel] All right then,
show of hands, who's alive?

1514
01:04:07,867 --> 01:04:08,800
Oh, I'm sorry.

1515
01:04:10,267 --> 01:04:11,967
- [Tom] I am not
cleaning this up.

1516
01:04:13,200 --> 01:04:14,567
- [Crow] Wow,
crowd's dead tonight,

1517
01:04:14,600 --> 01:04:16,467
typical Friday late show.
- Mm-hmm.

1518
01:04:18,067 --> 01:04:20,533
Man, this kinda took
a really dark turn.

1519
01:04:20,567 --> 01:04:22,033
- Where?
- Cripes, I'm in trouble,

1520
01:04:22,067 --> 01:04:23,567
I'm gonna get blamed for this.

1521
01:04:25,633 --> 01:04:27,633
Oop, pardon me, excuse me,
sorry about the head there.

1522
01:04:27,667 --> 01:04:30,000
Sorry, oh, pardon me.
- Oh no, those guys too.

1523
01:04:31,600 --> 01:04:33,667
- [Joel] Well, this
could've gone better.

1524
01:04:34,667 --> 01:04:37,600
(mysterious music)

1525
01:04:43,200 --> 01:04:45,367
- [Tom] All right, go ahead,
everything checks out.

1526
01:04:48,367 --> 01:04:50,567
- Antinea!
- I'm in the shower.

1527
01:04:50,600 --> 01:04:52,300
- [Joel] Herc is as mad as heck

1528
01:04:52,333 --> 01:04:54,100
and he's not gonna
take it anymore!

1529
01:04:56,167 --> 01:04:59,467
- [Hercules] Where's my
son, where's Androcles?

1530
01:04:59,500 --> 01:05:01,000
- Have no fear.
- Underdog is here!

1531
01:05:01,033 --> 01:05:04,000
- Your son is alive, he is safe.

1532
01:05:04,967 --> 01:05:06,700
- Why didn't you
have him killed?

1533
01:05:06,733 --> 01:05:09,033
- That was part of the deal!
- Why did you spare him?

1534
01:05:09,067 --> 01:05:12,067
(suspenseful music)

1535
01:05:14,267 --> 01:05:16,967
- Oh, hi.
- Because of you, Hercules.

1536
01:05:17,000 --> 01:05:20,200
Listen to me, I could
have had your son killed

1537
01:05:20,233 --> 01:05:21,867
and with him your friend.

1538
01:05:21,900 --> 01:05:25,767
I could've had you killed too.
- I just didn't feel like it.

1539
01:05:25,800 --> 01:05:28,733
- Perhaps I should have.
- Hindsight's 20/20 sometimes.

1540
01:05:28,767 --> 01:05:31,467
- For that is what
mt people advised me.

1541
01:05:31,500 --> 01:05:33,300
But I did not heed their advice.

1542
01:05:35,867 --> 01:05:37,500
- [Crow] You're on my dress.

1543
01:05:38,633 --> 01:05:39,767
- I wanted you to live.

1544
01:05:41,200 --> 01:05:43,467
I wanted you to live
because I love you.

1545
01:05:43,500 --> 01:05:44,733
- [Crow] Long time.

1546
01:05:44,767 --> 01:05:46,233
- [Joel] I'm sorry,
I wasn't listening.

1547
01:05:46,267 --> 01:05:48,700
- If you will join me in
the conquest of the world,

1548
01:05:50,033 --> 01:05:53,200
all mankind will recognize
me as their queen.

1549
01:05:53,233 --> 01:05:56,233
And adore you as the
one and only god.

1550
01:05:56,267 --> 01:05:58,767
Love me, Hercules, and together

1551
01:05:58,800 --> 01:06:00,733
we shall reign
over men and gods.

1552
01:06:00,767 --> 01:06:03,033
- [Joel] Well it sounds
good, I'm interested,

1553
01:06:03,067 --> 01:06:04,300
but can I sleep on it?

1554
01:06:07,533 --> 01:06:08,900
- [Crow] You taste
like Alan Steel.

1555
01:06:08,933 --> 01:06:10,667
- [Tom] You taste
like Yvonne De Carlo.

1556
01:06:10,700 --> 01:06:12,433
- [Joel] Wait a minute,
now you can have both.

1557
01:06:12,467 --> 01:06:14,067
- Hmm.
(smacking lips)

1558
01:06:14,100 --> 01:06:15,000
Go great together.

1559
01:06:16,533 --> 01:06:18,433
- And how do you expect
to conquer the world?

1560
01:06:18,467 --> 01:06:19,767
- [Joel] Mass mailings
and basically,

1561
01:06:19,800 --> 01:06:22,600
you just saturate the market.

1562
01:06:22,633 --> 01:06:25,200
(somber music)

1563
01:06:27,700 --> 01:06:30,100
(vocalizing)

1564
01:06:31,700 --> 01:06:35,167
♪ Swing American ♪

1565
01:06:35,200 --> 01:06:38,367
- [Crow] Oh, plastiface,
that is a plan, I get it.

1566
01:06:38,400 --> 01:06:41,200
- These are my soldiers, my men,

1567
01:06:41,233 --> 01:06:44,267
against which no force
in the world can combat.

1568
01:06:44,300 --> 01:06:47,533
Of a supreme race, born
of the blood of Uranus.

1569
01:06:47,567 --> 01:06:49,667
(groaning)
- You've crossed the line!

1570
01:06:49,700 --> 01:06:52,133
- Pick up that table, Hercules,

1571
01:06:52,167 --> 01:06:53,867
and hurl it away
if you're able to.

1572
01:06:53,900 --> 01:06:56,800
- [Joel] Heh, no problem,
do it all the time.

1573
01:06:59,400 --> 01:07:00,900
(grunting)
- Table for two?

1574
01:07:02,200 --> 01:07:05,200
(suspenseful music)

1575
01:07:08,100 --> 01:07:10,867
- [Tom] Sumpter will
throw the table now.

1576
01:07:10,900 --> 01:07:13,900
(suspenseful music)

1577
01:07:17,167 --> 01:07:19,633
- With this new race I
can dominate the world.

1578
01:07:19,667 --> 01:07:22,033
- [Joel] We'll break
tables all over the world!

1579
01:07:23,067 --> 01:07:24,333
- This is a mad dream, Antinea,

1580
01:07:24,367 --> 01:07:26,267
but I shall put an
end to the madness.

1581
01:07:27,467 --> 01:07:28,700
- [Joel] Uh-oh.

1582
01:07:32,900 --> 01:07:34,000
- [Crow] Ooh!

1583
01:07:36,800 --> 01:07:38,333
(vocalizing)

1584
01:07:38,367 --> 01:07:40,100
- [Joel] Oh, that was kinda
dumb, locking myself in,

1585
01:07:40,133 --> 01:07:41,900
I didn't think that
through at all.

1586
01:07:43,633 --> 01:07:45,000
- And he aims!
- No he doesn't.

1587
01:07:45,033 --> 01:07:47,700
- Oh.
- I don't think so.

1588
01:07:47,733 --> 01:07:49,900
(gong ringing)

1589
01:07:49,933 --> 01:07:53,800
- [Joel] Send in the
reinforcements, we
need reinforcements!

1590
01:07:53,833 --> 01:07:55,467
- [Tom] All right,
Johnson's at the plate,

1591
01:07:55,500 --> 01:07:59,033
he's a swift hitter, oh it's
a swing and a line drive!

1592
01:07:59,067 --> 01:08:00,067
- [Crow] That's it?

1593
01:08:02,267 --> 01:08:03,100
Oh.

1594
01:08:09,400 --> 01:08:11,000
- [All] Surprise!

1595
01:08:11,867 --> 01:08:13,200
- [Joel] Uh-oh SpaghettiOs.

1596
01:08:14,767 --> 01:08:17,167
- [Crow] They're all photo
negatives of Abe Lincoln.

1597
01:08:18,467 --> 01:08:21,167
- [Joel] Just take a
little off the sides.

1598
01:08:21,200 --> 01:08:22,100
- Hercules.

1599
01:08:23,300 --> 01:08:24,633
- [Joel] Well there's Ol Yeller.

1600
01:08:24,667 --> 01:08:27,167
(chuckling)

1601
01:08:27,200 --> 01:08:29,433
- [Crow] We've come to
your emotional rescue.

1602
01:08:31,433 --> 01:08:32,533
- [Joel] Hey look, behind him,

1603
01:08:32,567 --> 01:08:34,933
there's the Millennium Falcon.

1604
01:08:34,967 --> 01:08:38,600
(mysterious music)

1605
01:08:38,633 --> 01:08:40,267
- [Crow] It's The Police.

1606
01:08:41,900 --> 01:08:45,100
- [Tom] So I guess I'll just
be sending out an SOS, guys.

1607
01:08:45,133 --> 01:08:47,167
(laughing)

1608
01:08:47,200 --> 01:08:50,000
- [Crow] Wow, these guys can
stare down the best of 'em.

1609
01:08:51,167 --> 01:08:52,500
- [Joel] It's funny
if you think about it,

1610
01:08:52,533 --> 01:08:54,033
you know, queenie?

1611
01:08:55,567 --> 01:08:59,033
♪ We represent the
Lollipop Guild ♪

1612
01:08:59,067 --> 01:09:01,467
- [Tom] I'll hit you with my
giant swab, I swear I'll do it.

1613
01:09:01,500 --> 01:09:03,467
- [Crow] Charles Schwab?

1614
01:09:03,500 --> 01:09:05,600
- [Joel] What makes
those guys so scary?

1615
01:09:06,733 --> 01:09:08,200
- [Tom] They're super
strong, you know?

1616
01:09:08,233 --> 01:09:09,533
- [Crow] You've
been following this?

1617
01:09:16,333 --> 01:09:19,167
(doors whooshing)

1618
01:09:22,467 --> 01:09:24,033
- Oh hi, friends,
what you doin'?

1619
01:09:24,067 --> 01:09:25,133
- We made a Hercules
action figure!

1620
01:09:25,167 --> 01:09:26,500
- Oh wow.
- It does all kinds of

1621
01:09:26,533 --> 01:09:28,900
really cool stuff.
- Yeah, it can pick stuff up

1622
01:09:28,933 --> 01:09:30,300
over its head and throw it!

1623
01:09:31,700 --> 01:09:33,633
- And it does lots of
other cool stuff too.

1624
01:09:33,667 --> 01:09:36,367
It lies down and sleeps
for hours on end.

1625
01:09:38,267 --> 01:09:39,833
- Wow, it's really
neat, isn't it?

1626
01:09:39,867 --> 01:09:41,833
Just the way it lies there.

1627
01:09:41,867 --> 01:09:44,267
- Well you guys, I hate
to be critical but--

1628
01:09:44,300 --> 01:09:46,467
- No, no, we haven't even
told you the coolest part yet!

1629
01:09:46,500 --> 01:09:47,700
- It talks!
- Yeah!

1630
01:09:47,733 --> 01:09:49,567
- Oh, wow, really?

1631
01:09:49,600 --> 01:09:51,667
Well that's a Herc of a
different color isn't it?

1632
01:09:51,700 --> 01:09:53,567
- Yeah.
- Come on in, okay.

1633
01:09:53,600 --> 01:09:55,267
Let's see, why didn't you tell
me that in the first place?

1634
01:09:55,300 --> 01:09:57,367
I bet he says a lot
of neat action stuff.

1635
01:09:57,400 --> 01:10:00,000
- [Hercules] I'm so sleepy I
can barely keep my eyes open.

1636
01:10:00,033 --> 01:10:01,733
(laughing)
- Oh but I wanna hear

1637
01:10:01,767 --> 01:10:04,600
the kinda stuff he says when
he's runnin' into battle.

1638
01:10:04,633 --> 01:10:07,533
- [Hercules] I'm so sleepy I
can barely keep my eyes open.

1639
01:10:08,933 --> 01:10:11,900
- Are you sure you wanna
call this an action figure?

1640
01:10:11,933 --> 01:10:13,400
(sighing)

1641
01:10:13,433 --> 01:10:15,700
- [Hercules] I'm so sleepy I
can barely keep my eyes open.

1642
01:10:15,733 --> 01:10:17,967
(crying)
- I admit it, I admit it,

1643
01:10:18,000 --> 01:10:21,200
a Hercules action figure
is lame, really lame!

1644
01:10:21,233 --> 01:10:23,600
- We're failures,
total failures!

1645
01:10:23,633 --> 01:10:26,600
- Oh, no, come on
you guys, come on,

1646
01:10:26,633 --> 01:10:29,400
you put your best foot forward.

1647
01:10:29,433 --> 01:10:31,533
- I don't even have a foot!
- Okay, okay,

1648
01:10:31,567 --> 01:10:33,767
okay, that's beside
the point, okay?

1649
01:10:33,800 --> 01:10:36,200
You guys tried your very hardest

1650
01:10:36,233 --> 01:10:37,667
and you did the
very best you could

1651
01:10:37,700 --> 01:10:40,033
and because of that
you'll never be failures.

1652
01:10:40,067 --> 01:10:42,633
(sniffling)

1653
01:10:42,667 --> 01:10:44,767
- [Hercules] You're absolutely
right, Joel Robinson,

1654
01:10:44,800 --> 01:10:46,867
we'll be back after
this commercial message

1655
01:10:46,900 --> 01:10:49,500
from Jolly Rancher
candies, good night now.

1656
01:10:49,533 --> 01:10:51,800
(groaning)
(thudding)

1657
01:10:51,833 --> 01:10:54,400
(upbeat music)

1658
01:10:56,600 --> 01:10:58,067
(mysterious music)

1659
01:10:58,100 --> 01:10:59,500
- You okay?
- Mm-hmm.

1660
01:10:59,533 --> 01:11:01,367
- [Tom] Pretty funny.

1661
01:11:01,400 --> 01:11:05,200
- [Crow] Oh, that's no
way to treat my hinder!

1662
01:11:07,367 --> 01:11:08,200
- Father!

1663
01:11:09,333 --> 01:11:11,167
- Hylas!
- Interruptus.

1664
01:11:11,200 --> 01:11:12,200
- [Tom] Ooh.

1665
01:11:13,367 --> 01:11:14,767
- And so once again
you have disobeyed me.

1666
01:11:14,800 --> 01:11:16,500
- [Tom] Once again we see
there's nothing you can possess

1667
01:11:16,533 --> 01:11:18,700
that I cannot take away.
- Wanted to attack the city

1668
01:11:18,733 --> 01:11:20,600
and there wasn't any
time to stop them.

